+# L2Vzla Server Emulator — Build Notes
+
+## What this is
+
+- **Pack:** aCis rev 409 (Lineage 2 Interlude, free/open-source pack, package root `net.sf.l2j`)
+- **Source repo:** https://github.com/DEVjEXTREME/L2jaCis-409 (mirror of the aCis 409 gameserver + datapack; the original Tryskell/aCis GitHub repo is no longer public)
+- **Built:** 2026-07-23 with **OpenJDK 21.0.10** (`/opt/homebrew/opt/openjdk@21`) and **Apache Ant 1.10.15**
+  (ant was already installed via Homebrew). Build was clean, zero errors, 2343 source files.
+- **Build command** (from each module dir): `JAVA_HOME=/opt/homebrew/opt/openjdk@21 ant`
+  (default targets: `dist` for the gameserver, `build` for the datapack)
+
+## Directory layout
+
+```
+server/                          # git clone of DEVjEXTREME/L2jaCis-409
+├── aCis_gameserver/             # Java source module
+│   ├── java/net/sf/l2j/...      # source (loginserver, gameserver, accountmanager, gsregistering)
+│   ├── config/                  # source configs (copied into dist by ant)
+│   ├── lib/mariadb-java-client-3.1.4.jar   # only runtime dependency
+│   └── build/                   # ant output
+│       ├── l2jserver.jar        # compiled jar (both servers in one jar)
+│       └── dist/                # ★ DEPLOYABLE TREE ★
+│           ├── login/           # LOGIN SERVER (run from here)
+│           │   ├── libs/l2jserver.jar + mariadb-java-client-3.1.4.jar
+│           │   ├── config/{loginserver,logging,banned_ips}.properties
+│           │   ├── serverNames.xml          # copied here from datapack (loginserver reads ./serverNames.xml)
+│           │   ├── startLoginServer.sh  → LoginServer_loop.sh (auto-restart loop)
+│           │   ├── RegisterGameServer.sh  # generates gameserver hexid
+│           │   └── startSQLAccountManager.sh
+│           ├── gameserver/      # GAME SERVER (run from here)
+│           │   ├── libs/        (same jars)
+│           │   ├── config/{server,players,npcs,clans,events,siege,geoengine,logging}.properties
+│           │   ├── data/        # datapack content (xml, html, geodata dir, serverNames.xml)
+│           │   └── startGameServer.sh → GameServer_loop.sh (auto-restart loop, exit code 2 = reboot)
+│           ├── sql/             # 65 .sql files, one per table
+│           └── tools/           # database_installer.sh / full_install.sql / gs_install.sql
+└── aCis_datapack/               # datapack source (data/, sql/, tools/) + its own ant build in build/
+```
+
+Runtime main classes (both in `l2jserver.jar`):
+- Login: `net.sf.l2j.loginserver.LoginServer`
+- Game: `net.sf.l2j.gameserver.GameServer`
+- GS registration: `net.sf.l2j.gsregistering.GameServerRegister`
+- Account manager: `net.sf.l2j.accountmanager.SQLAccountManager`
+
+## What the next phase (DB setup + config + first run) needs to know
+
+1. **Database:** pack uses MariaDB/MySQL via `mariadb-java-client`. Defaults (in
+   `login/config/loginserver.properties` and `gameserver/config/server.properties`):
+   `URL = jdbc:mariadb://localhost/acis`, `Login = root`, empty password, database name `acis`.
+   Homebrew MariaDB is installed but **not started** yet. Create DB `acis`, then install tables with
+   `dist/tools/database_installer.sh` (or `full_install.sql`; `gs_install.sql` is the gameserver-only subset).
+2. **Game server registration:** after the DB is up, run `login/RegisterGameServer.sh` to create a hexid,
+   then name the server in `gameserver/data/serverNames.xml` (default list ships retail names, ids 1–127).
+3. **Ports:** login 2106 (client) / 9014 (GS↔LS), gameserver 7777. `AutoCreateAccounts = True` already.
+4. **Geodata:** **NO geodata files are included** (aCis ships geodata separately). `geoengine.properties`
+   has `GeoDataType = L2OFF`, path `./data/geodata/` (only contains a Readme + a map jpg). The server runs
+   without geodata but pathing/geo checks will be off; obtaining L2OFF-format Interlude geodata is a
+   separate task. Readme: `aCis_datapack/data/geodata/Readme.txt`.
+5. **Start:** `cd dist/login && ./startLoginServer.sh`, `cd dist/gameserver && ./startGameServer.sh`
+   (both spawn loop scripts in background; logs in each `log/` dir). Not started in this phase.
+6. **Java on PATH:** start scripts call plain `java`; ensure `JAVA_HOME=/opt/homebrew/opt/openjdk@21`
+   is exported (or PATH prepended) when launching.
+
+## QoL / bot-friendly feature status (for the config-tuning phase)
+
+- **Autoloot:** built in — `gameserver/config/server.properties`: `AutoLoot`, `AutoLootRaid`,
+  `AutoLootHerbs` (all `False` by default).
+- **Buff slots:** `gameserver/config/players.properties` → `MaxBuffsAmount = 20` (default);
+  Divine Inspiration adds 4 more.
+- **Offline shops:** **Custom Java mod implemented** (see 'Custom mods' below) — config keys in
+  `gameserver/config/players.properties` (`OfflineTradeEnable`, `OfflineCraftEnable`, `OfflineRestoreOnLogin`).
+- **Voice commands (.menu etc.):** **Custom Java mod implemented** (see 'Custom mods' below) —
+  `.menu`, `.autoloot`, `.expon`/`.expoff`, `.offline`.
+- **Anti-bot:** no anti-automation blocking present in aCis by default (good for the project's
+  bot-friendly philosophy).
+
+## Verification done
+
+- `ant` builds succeeded for both modules (BUILD SUCCESSFUL).
+- Smoke test: launched `net.sf.l2j.loginserver.LoginServer` from `dist/login` — configs loaded,
+  RSA/Blowfish keys cached, game-server manager started; the only failure was
+  `Unknown database 'acis'` (expected: DB not created yet) and a missing `./serverNames.xml`,
+  which was then copied into `dist/login/`. No servers were left running.
+
+## Notes
+
+- The jar manifest lists `Main-Class: net.sf.l2j.Server`, which does not exist in the source —
+  harmless, since the loop scripts invoke the real main classes via `-cp`.
+- Login loop script uses `nice -n -2`, which may warn without privileges on macOS; harmless.
+- `server/.git` still points at the upstream mirror; another phase may want to fold `server/`
+  into the project's own git repo or re-init.
+
+## Custom mods
+
+Added 2026-07-23 (Java mods, compiled into `l2jserver.jar`, 2346 source files, build clean).
+All sources under `aCis_gameserver/java/net/sf/l2j/gameserver/` unless noted.
+
+### 1. Offline shops (offline trade)
+
+- **Behavior:** any logout path (Logout/Restart packets, connection loss, `.offline`) with an
+  active private store (buy/sell, or craft if enabled) keeps the Player in the world as an
+  **offline trader**: client detached, DB `online=0`, character + store saved. The store keeps
+  operating. Package-sale stores are never kept offline. Server shutdown saves and removes
+  offline traders normally (`Shutdown.disconnectAllPlayers`).
+- **Login restore:** on next login, `GameClient.loadCharFromDisk` recycles the offline-trader
+  instance when `OfflineRestoreOnLogin = True` (store closed, stands up, instant login at the
+  same spot). If `False`, the trader is saved/removed and the first login attempt aborts
+  (re-select the character to enter, stock aCis behavior).
+- **Config** (`config/players.properties`, copied to dist on build): `OfflineTradeEnable` (True),
+  `OfflineCraftEnable` (True), `OfflineRestoreOnLogin` (True). Declared/loaded in
+  `java/net/sf/l2j/Config.java` (`OFFLINE_TRADE_ENABLE`, `OFFLINE_CRAFT_ENABLE`,
+  `OFFLINE_RESTORE_ON_LOGIN`).
+- **Code:** `model/actor/Player.java` → `_isOfflineTrader`, `isOfflineTrader()`,
+  `canOpenOfflineShop()`, `becomeOfflineTrader()`, `stopOfflineTrade()` (after
+  `isInManageStoreMode()`); `network/GameClient.java` → `CleanupTask` (offline decision) and
+  `loadCharFromDisk` (restore-on-login).
+
+### 2. Voiced commands + .menu
+
+- **Infra (new, follows aCis handler conventions):** `handler/IVoicedCommandHandler.java`,
+  `handler/VoicedCommandHandler.java` (auto-scans `handler/voicedcommandhandlers/` via
+  `AbstractHandler`), `handler/voicedcommandhandlers/Menu.java` (registers `menu`, `autoloot`,
+  `expon`, `expoff`, `offline`). Hooked in `network/clientpackets/Say2.java` (chat text starting
+  with `.`) and `RequestBypassToServer.java` (`voiced_` bypass links used by the menu HTML).
+  Handler count is logged at startup in `GameServer.java` ("Loaded N voiced command handlers.").
+- **`.menu`:** HTML window (`data/html/mods/menu.htm`, + `info.htm` for the message-of-the-day /
+  server info page, both in Spanish) with bypass toggles. A one-line welcome message pointing to
+  `.menu` is sent in `EnterWorld.java`.
+- **Autoloot toggle:** per-player, persisted in `character_memo` (`autoloot` key) via
+  `PlayerMemo`. `Player.isAutoLoot()/isAutoLootRaid()/isAutoLootHerbs()` return the memo value or
+  fall back to the global `AutoLoot*` configs. `Monster.dropOrAutoLootItem/dropOrAutoLootHerb`
+  now use those per-player getters (party/raid distribution logic unchanged).
+- **.expon/.expoff:** per-player exp block, memo key `expBlocked`. `Player.addExpAndSp` (both
+  overloads) zeroes positive exp when blocked; SP gain and deleveling (negative exp) still apply.
+- **.offline:** requires an active private store; calls `player.logout(true)`, the regular
+  offline-trade flow keeps the trader in the world.
+- **Note:** rebuilds run `ant clean` first, which wipes `build/dist` — after every gameserver
+  rebuild, re-merge datapack data (`rsync -a aCis_datapack/build/gameserver/data/
+  aCis_gameserver/build/dist/gameserver/data/`) and re-copy `serverNames.xml` into `dist/login/`
+  (both done after the 2026-07-23 rebuild).
+
+### Verification
+
+- `ant` builds: gameserver + datapack both BUILD SUCCESSFUL, zero errors.
+- jshell check against `build/l2jserver.jar`: `VoicedCommandHandler.getInstance().size() == 5`,
+  `menu`/`offline`/`expon` resolve to the `Menu` handler (jar package scan works).
+- Not yet tested: in-game flow (needs running server + client; part of the smoke-test phase).
